  "answer_text": "It looks like there are several pools named \"Glenwood Pool\" across the United States! Here's a summary of the most notable ones:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 1. **Glenwood Pool \u2013 Forest Glen, Maryland**\nGlenwood Pool is a swim club set back among the trees and along a creek in historic Forest Glen, Maryland. You can contact them at board@glenwoodpool.org for more information.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf0a 2. **Glenwood Hot Springs Resort \u2013 Glenwood Springs, Colorado**\nGlenwood Hot Springs Resort has more than 7 expansive pools on the property, including the original historic pool which is the \"world's largest hot springs pool.\" The historic thermal spring water has been drawing visitors from all over the world since 1888.\n\n- The source of the mineral water is the Yampah Spring, which produces over 3.5 million gallons of water per day at a temperature of 122\u00b0F.\n- The Grand Pool contains over 1 million gallons of water and is an aquatic playing field for kids of all ages.\n- When you purchase Day Pool Passes online, you will be able to visit the pool immediately or select a future date. You can also purchase passes at the pool entrance on the day of arrival.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 3. **Glenwood Aquatic Center \u2013 Glenwood Springs, Colorado (City Recreation)**\nThis 277,000-gallon pool boasts 8 lap lanes and a one-meter diving board. The pool ranges from 4 feet deep to 12 feet deep, and temperature is kept between 82\u201384 degrees.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 4. **Glenwood Houses Pool \u2013 Brooklyn, New York**\nIf you find yourself in the Glenwood Houses neighborhood of Brooklyn, New York, this pool offers a place to cool off and enjoy the water during hot New York summers. Managed by NYC Parks, you can expect a well-maintained facility that caters to the community's aquatic needs.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 5. **Glenwood Pool \u2013 Columbus, Ohio**\nGlenwood Pool in Columbus is open for the season starting May 23. Hours are Monday\u2013Friday: 1\u20137 p.m., Saturday: 12\u20136 p.m., and Sunday: 12\u20136 p.m.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 6. **Glennwood Pool \u2013 Evans, Georgia**\nGlennwood Pool is a non-profit, volunteer-run neighborhood pool in Evans, Georgia, offering memberships for residents and non-residents, seasonal events like dive-in movie nights, and military & senior discounts.\n\n---\n\nCould you let me know which **Glenwood Pool** you're interested in, or what city/state you're in? I'd be happy to give you more specific details! \ud83d\ude0a",
